    "answer": {
      "short": "$I=\\dfrac{180(n-2)}{n}^\\circ=\\left(180-\\dfrac{360}{n}\\right)^\\circ$.",
      "worked": "The interior angle sum is $180(n-2)^\\circ$. All $n$ interior angles of a regular polygon are equal, so\n\n$\\begin{align*}I&=\\frac{180(n-2)}{n}^\\circ\\\\I&=\\left(180-\\frac{360}{n}\\right)^\\circ.\\end{align*}$",
